onted with large-scale suffering, contrasting it with our deep empathy for an identifiable victim. My goal is to bridge this gap in our emotional response to foster more equitable global care.\n\n**Modifying human reflexes**\n\nI'm reconsidering my approach to empathy, realizing that directly amplifying grief for distant suffering could be detrimental. My focus has shifted to eliminating the reflex to dehumanize others and making intellectual honesty a source of relief, not distress.\n\n",
